  "id": "good-death",
  "term": "good death",
  "definition": "In this context, good death refers to a desirable quality of dying at the end of life and is treated as an outcome that palliative care aims to support. It is also something that can be evaluated from family members’ perspectives as an indicator of end-of-life care quality.",
